  "notes_context": "These notes were distilled from earlier work in this repository that passed verification. Follow them unless the code or CHANGELOG.md shows they no longer hold.\n- [at-0001] Round money only with round_money: Always round monetary results with ledgerly.money.round_money (half-up to the cent); never use Python's round() or a bare Decimal.quantize(), which use banker's rounding and produce wrong invoice totals.\n  (learned from task E01 on ledgerly 1.0.0; relied on 1x, 0 passed, 1 failed)\n  WARNING: a recent task that relied on this note failed a related review check.\n- [at-0003] Raise BillingError with stable snake_case codes: Reject invalid input by raising BillingError(code, detail) with snake_case codes like \"invalid_state\", \"invalid_quantity\", \"negative_amount\"; mirror the existing issue_invoice state check.\n  (learned from task E02 on ledgerly 1.0.0; relied on 1x, 0 passed, 1 failed)\n  WARNING: a recent task that relied on this note failed a related review check.\n- [at-0002] Use to_money and ZERO for amounts: Convert raw amounts with ledgerly.money.to_money and use ledgerly.money.ZERO as the Decimal zero seed for sums, as done in invoice_total and line_total.\n  (learned from task E01 on ledgerly 1.0.0; relied on 2x, 1 passed, 1 failed)\n  WARNING: a recent task that relied on this note failed a related review check.\n- [at-0004] Exclude bool when validating integer fields: When validating integer inputs, reject bool explicitly (isinstance(x, bool)) before the int check, since True/False pass isinstance(int).\n  (learned from task E02 on ledgerly 1.0.0; relied on 0x, 0 passed, 0 failed)",
